WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.560
- Clean your ass, next question.

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:04.000
(gentle music)
- Hi, my name is Marie,

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.480
I'm Lebanese American.

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:06.880
- Hey, I'm Laila,

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:08.880
I'm Lebanese-Palestinian-American.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.160
- Hi, I'm comedian Alyssa
Dookhi, I'm from Kuwait.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:14.320
- My name is Michael
Kamel, I'm Palestinian

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:15.960
and today I'm going to be answering

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:19.440
commonly Googled questions about, Arabs.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:22.333
Is it Arab or is it Arabic?

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.300
- Arab? Me, I am Arab.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:29.770
The language is Arabic.
Dance move is arabesque.

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:31.640
A coffee is Arabica.

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:35.010
- Arab is the people.
Arabic is the language.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:37.240
- Arab is a people.
Arabic is the language.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:39.750
I am Arab and my family speaks Arabic.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:42.140
- It's a language and then the people.

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:44.130
I'm right on that, right? That's right.

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:46.130
Yeah, like yeah.

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:48.103
Is Arab the same as Middle Eastern?

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:51.550
- Arabs are Middle Eastern

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:53.490
but Middle Eastern doesn't equal Arab.

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:57.590
- It's kind of like that thing
of, a square is a rectangle

00:00:57.590 --> 00:01:00.000
but a...
No or whatever it is.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.000
Middle Eastern is a blanket term

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.240
for like many different ethnicities.

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:07.050
- You can be Persian. You can be a Syrian.

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:08.860
You can be Kurdish.

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:10.690
A lot of the language
around the Middle East

00:01:10.690 --> 00:01:13.470
and Arabs is really complicated and loaded

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:14.970
and it comes with a lot of baggage.

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:16.730
- That's one reason why I like to say

00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:18.720
Southwest Asia and North Africa.

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:20.730
It connects us all through the things

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:22.820
that keep us similar while focusing more

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:24.600
on a geographical location.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:27.450
Are Arabs considered white?

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:31.610
- Oh, I knew this question
was gonna come up.

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:34.220
- If you ask me, I'm not white.

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:36.940
- I personally do not
consider myself white

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:38.720
and people generally

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:41.900
get that I'm from some
Middle Eastern area.

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:45.310
There are Arabs who are
white or who look white.

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:47.700
So for example, I have
people in my extended family

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.480
that have blonde hair and blue eyes

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:50.860
and if you didn't know their names,

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:53.240
you would not think they were Arab at all.

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:55.520
- According to the U.S. Census,

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:58.970
Arabs are meant to check
the white category.

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:03.250
- When Arabs first came
to the U.S. in 1870s,

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:07.900
pushed out of Greater
Syria by the Ottomans

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:12.170
and had to prove, because
of the Exclusion Act,

00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:14.110
that they were not Asians

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:15.940
and could stay in this country.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:19.030
So those people said, "Look at
us, we're from the Holy Land,

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:22.690
we're Christians, we could be white."

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:25.800
- Decades later, the
diversity of Arabs in the U.S.

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:29.380
has been much more expanded

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:31.560
and so it's been really problematic

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:33.740
because the U.S. Census
doesn't account for who we are.

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:35.790
We're a much larger population

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:37.620
that can't accurately be measured

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:39.760
because the census doesn't
have a category for us,

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:41.750
so we get lumped in
with those who are white

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:44.440
and so now there is a
concerted effort by activists

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:47.330
and advocates all around the
country to have designation

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:50.100
for people who identify as being Arab

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:51.720
or more broadly, Middle Eastern.

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:53.470
- [Alyssa] Why do Arabs use bidets?

00:02:54.808 --> 00:02:57.710
(Marie gasps)
(Marie laughs)

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:00.650
- I have been wanting one,
but it doesn't have anything

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:01.483
to do with me being Arab.

00:03:01.483 --> 00:03:03.430
- For the Arabs that are Muslim

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:05.943
they do use bidets in order to be clean,

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:08.901
'specially before prayer
and for the rest of us

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:11.600
'specially Lebanese,
it's cause we bougie A-F.

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:13.400
- Because you have to wash your ass.

00:03:15.244 --> 00:03:16.650
(man chuckles)
Like...

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:19.460
- Clean your ass. Next question.

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:21.203
- [Laila] Do Arabs eat pork?

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:24.540
- This Arab does.
Do not show this video

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:27.360
to my dad but many Arabs do.

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:29.640
Not all Arabs come from religions

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:31.260
that prohibit eating pork.

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:33.650
- Don't worry about what
I'm eating (laughs).

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:35.900
- [Michael] What do Arabs wear?

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:37.805
- Arabs We're all sorts of stuff.

00:03:37.805 --> 00:03:40.490
These are funny, like (laughs).

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:44.290
- Well today I'm wearing
just a black T-shirt

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:47.580
and some shorts that I actually cut up

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:49.630
because these were pants that
I didn't really want anymore

00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:50.890
but I didn't want them to go to waste.

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:53.680
So that's what this Arab wears.

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:54.810
- Depends on the region.

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:58.470
There's lots of different
clothing that is indigenous

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:00.210
to each different place.

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:03.440
I mean, there's a huge part of the planet

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:06.430
covered by Arab countries,
so in each different place

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:07.890
people wear all sorts of different things.

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:10.330
And then, don't forget, there
are Arabs in the Diaspora

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:12.410
who are wearing whatever
it's normal to wear

00:04:12.410 --> 00:04:13.260
where they live.

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:15.203
- Is Arab the same as Persian?

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:18.550
No, Arab is not the same as Persian.

00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:20.940
- Persians are people that come from Iran.

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:24.100
Iran is in the Middle East, but
Iran is not an Arab country.

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:25.140
- I get this question a lot

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:27.363
especially as a Palestinian,
people are always like,

00:04:27.363 --> 00:04:29.920
" Oh, are you Persian
or are you Pakistanian?"

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:31.500
No, no, no.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:33.030
Persian, Pakistani

00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:36.070
and Palestinian are three
different ethnicities,

00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:37.635
three different locations.

00:04:37.635 --> 00:04:41.410
- [Laila] Do all Arab
countries speak Arabic?

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:43.110
- I actually don't know
this and I'm not gonna claim

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:45.610
to know this, but I'm
assuming like yes and...

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:48.700
Most Arab countries speak Arabic,

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:50.680
but often there's like French influence

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:53.140
and often they're educated
in English as well.

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:55.240
- All Arab countries speak Arabic,

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:57.730
but in most of Arab countries

00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:00.210
especially those who have been occupied

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:03.600
or colonized by other
countries in their history,

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:05.480
there's several different
languages spoken.

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:08.760
- There's usually another
primary language along with it.

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:10.900
Sometimes that's an indigenous language

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:13.760
and a lot of North Africa
there are so many cool

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:14.593
different languages.

00:05:14.593 --> 00:05:16.060
I highly encourage you to check out

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:16.960
and learn about.

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:18.823
where do Arabs come from?

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:22.060
- Arabs come from a lot of places.

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:23.530
- A magical place.

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:26.400
- When a mommy Arab and a daddy Arab

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:28.760
love each other very much.

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:30.017
- Our mothers wombs (chuckles).

00:05:30.017 --> 00:05:30.850
(baby coos)

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:33.220
- They can come from
the Gulf, North Africa,

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:34.980
Sudan, the Levant.

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:38.160
- And there's Arabs in America
that are born in America.

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:39.720
They're from all over.

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:42.510
- [Michael] What does Arab American mean?

00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:44.250
- This means so many things
to so many different people.

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:47.400
I'm Arab American because
my mom is from America

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:48.570
and my dad is Arab.

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:50.110
- I'm still 'tryna figure that out.

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:52.760
I'm still 'tryna figure out if I am...

00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:55.120
If I can call myself Arab American.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:58.190
- It also is that because
I'm an Arab in America.

00:05:58.190 --> 00:06:00.380
Some people distinguish
between Arab American

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:01.970
and Arabs in America.

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:03.900
- To me, Arab American means somebody

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:06.950
who considers themselves
both Arab and American

00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:10.040
in whatever capacity makes sense to them.

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:12.040
- Look I wear being Arab on my sleeve

00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:13.540
to the point where people probably think

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:14.947
I'm totally obnoxious.

00:06:14.947 --> 00:06:17.530
"Like we get it, you're Arab." (chuckles)

00:06:17.530 --> 00:06:19.390
- But I get kind of self-conscious feeling

00:06:19.390 --> 00:06:22.310
like, "Am I the right one to
educate this person on this?"

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:23.240
- In my experience,

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:25.640
these questions have come
from a place of curiosity.

00:06:25.640 --> 00:06:26.910
I'm glad that they feel safe enough

00:06:26.910 --> 00:06:29.030
to ask me those questions
and they wanna learn more.

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:30.830
- I would recommend asking
people for resources

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:33.747
if they have any, or
give it a quick Google.

